IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lrmp-survival`

-- Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1944 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in
-- lrmp-survival.l4. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the
-- encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`for the estate` MEANS `the person who had the claim, whose estate I act for`
`against the estate` MEANS `the person my claim is against`

`other` MEANS `any other cause of action`
`PRA claim` MEANS `a claim under Division 2 of Part 3 of the Property (Relationships) Act 1984`
`enticement` MEANS `inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other`
`promise` MEANS `breach of promise to marry`
`CtR` MEANS `a claim by relatives under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897`

`exemplary` MEANS `exemplary damages`
`lost years` MEANS `loss of earning capacity or earnings for the years after death the person would have lived but for the wrong`
`earnings to death` MEANS `loss of earnings or earning capacity up to the death`
`expenses` MEANS `medical, care and other expenses incurred before the death`
`pain` MEANS `pain or suffering, bodily or mental harm, or curtailment of expectation of life`
`funeral` MEANS `funeral expenses`
`death loss` MEANS `another loss to the estate because of the death`
`death gain` MEANS `a gain to the estate because of the death, such as insurance paid on death`
`promise damage` MEANS `damage to the estate flowing from a breach of promise to marry`

`left out` MEANS `left out: the estate's damages do not include it, or are worked out without it`
`not cut down` MEANS `not cut down by section 2(2): the estate recovers it if the cause of action gives it`
`funeral may be included` MEANS `funeral expenses may be included`
`no survival` MEANS `the claim does not survive for the estate, so there are no estate damages under this Act`
`not settled` MEANS `this Act does not settle it`

§§ `s 2(4) -- deemed cause of action`

-- Arguments: they died before or at the same time as the damage; a claim would have existed had they been alive.
#ASSERT `Is my claim deemed to have existed against them before they died` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim deemed to have existed against them before they died` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim deemed to have existed against them before they died` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim deemed to have existed against them before they died` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 2(1), (4), (5) -- survival`

-- Arguments: whose death, kind, died after commencement, cause of action existed at death, (s 2(4)) died before or with
-- the damage, (s 2(4)) would have had a claim.
-- An ordinary claim survives both ways.
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The proviso: each excepted kind, in each direction.
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `defamation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `defamation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `seduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `enticement` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `PRA claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `PRA claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The proviso beats the open questions (death before commencement; s 2(4) deeming).
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `PRA claim` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `defamation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A death before commencement is outside s 2(1) (fork F1).
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `other` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No cause of action subsisting at the death (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `other` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `other` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(4): the wrongdoer died before or with the damage; the deemed cause of action survives against the estate.
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `other` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `other` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `other` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(4) speaks only of a cause of action "against" the person who died: it does not help the estate side.
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `other` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(5): a Compensation to Relatives Act claim survives against the wrongdoer's estate; for the estate of a relative
-- who dies, s 2(1)'s "all causes of action" is read on its words (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `CtR` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `against the estate` `CtR` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `CtR` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Breach of promise to marry is not excepted: it survives (s 2(2)(b) limits the damages).
#ASSERT `Does the claim survive the death` `for the estate` `promise` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 2(2), (7) -- the estate's damages`

-- Arguments: kind, died after commencement, cause of action existed at death, death caused by the wrong, dust-related
-- condition, own proceedings pending before the Dust Diseases Tribunal at death, kind of damages.
-- s 2(2)(a)(i): exemplary damages, whether or not the wrong caused the death.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `exemplary` EQUALS `left out`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `exemplary` EQUALS `left out`
-- s 2(2)(a)(ii): the lost years.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `lost years` EQUALS `left out`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `lost years` EQUALS `left out`
-- Earnings and expenses up to the death: untouched.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `earnings to death` EQUALS `not cut down`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `earnings to death` EQUALS `not cut down`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `expenses` EQUALS `not cut down`
-- s 2(2)(d): pain and suffering etc. only where the wrong caused the death.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `pain` EQUALS `not cut down`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `pain` EQUALS `left out`
-- s 2(7) with s 12B(2) of the Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989: both conditions needed.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `pain` EQUALS `not cut down`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `pain` EQUALS `left out`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `pain` EQUALS `left out`
-- s 12B does not touch s 2(2)(a): exemplary damages are still left out in a dust case.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `exemplary` EQUALS `left out`
-- s 2(2)(c): losses and gains because of the death, with the funeral exception.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `funeral` EQUALS `funeral may be included`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `funeral` EQUALS `not settled`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `death loss` EQUALS `left out`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `death loss` EQUALS `not settled`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `death gain` EQUALS `left out`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `death gain` EQUALS `not settled`
-- The s 2(2)(b) head asked of another kind of claim (fork F5).
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `promise damage` EQUALS `not settled`
-- s 2(2)(b): breach of promise to marry is limited to damage to the estate flowing from the breach.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `promise` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `promise damage` EQUALS `not cut down`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `promise` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `earnings to death` EQUALS `left out`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `promise` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `pain` EQUALS `left out`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `promise` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `funeral` EQUALS `left out`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `promise` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `exemplary` EQUALS `left out`
-- No survival, or survival not settled.
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `defamation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `earnings to death` EQUALS `no survival`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `PRA claim` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `expenses` EQUALS `no survival`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `funeral` EQUALS `not settled`
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `other` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `funeral` EQUALS `not settled`
-- A relative's Compensation to Relatives Act claim surviving for the relative's own estate (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Can the estate recover these damages` `CtR` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `earnings to death` EQUALS `not cut down`

§§ `s 2(5), (6) -- other rights not cut down`

#ASSERT `Does the estate's claim cut down rights under that Act` `the dependants' claim under the Compensation to Relatives Act 1897` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the estate's claim cut down rights under that Act` `the Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Act 1942` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the estate's claim cut down rights under that Act` `the Transport Accidents Compensation Act 1987` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the estate's claim cut down rights under that Act` `the Motor Accidents Act 1988` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the estate's claim cut down rights under that Act` `another Act` EQUALS NOTHING
